WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.430
Targaryen civil war that divided Targaryen
dynasty and the entire Westeros in two, is

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.930
the main event of House of the Dragon.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:24.520
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.520
to air in 2022.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.930
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.899
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:37.320
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.970
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:47.260
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.019
Thats Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:54.219
The yet unreleased Fire And Vlood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:00:54.219 --> 00:01:00.160
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.640
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:10.420
Key event of the prequel will be the Dance
of the Dragon, a Targaryen civil war.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:16.070
It was a war of succession between Rhaenyra
(and her Blacks) and Aegon (and his Greens).

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:20.140
The blacks, previously known as the party
of the princess, were the faction of House

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.840
Targaryen and their loyalists who supported
the ascent of Rhaenyra Targaryen as Queen

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.710
of the Seven Kingdoms during the Dance of
the Dragons and the years that preceded it.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.909
They were opposed by the greens.

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:37.110
The title derives from a great tournament
held in 111 AC at King's Landing on the fifth

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:42.829
anniversary of King Viserys I's marriage to
Queen Alicent Hightower, his second wife.

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:48.340
At the opening feast, Queen Alicent wore a
green gown, whilst Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen,

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.659
Viserys's daughter by his first wife, dressed
dramatically in Targaryen red and black.

00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:57.871
Note was taken, and thereafter it became the
custom to refer to “greens” and “blacks”

00:01:57.871 --> 00:02:01.100
when talking of the queen’s party and the
party of the princess.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:06.130
Generally, Rhaenyra was supported by noble
families who had enjoyed royal favor during

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:12.370
her father's reign and possessed strong ties
to the crown, while Aegon II rallied those

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.080
who had been out of favor.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:20.250
Viserys I had signed charters with many powerful
Houses in which they swore to accept Rhaenyra

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.780
as his heir, but at least some of them broke
their word after Viserys died.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.811
Obviously the most prominent of the Blacks
is its leader and the person they are all

00:02:28.811 --> 00:02:31.210
fighting for, Rhaenyra Targaryen.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.640
Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen, cheered as the
Realm's Delight when she was young and later

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:41.190
called the Half-Year Queen, was the first-born
child of King Viserys I Targaryen.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:46.940
Rhaenyra was King Viserys I's only living
child by his first wife, Queen Aemma of House

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:47.940
Arryn.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.890
At the age of eight she was made her father's
heir and grew up expecting to become the first

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.260
ruling Queen of Westeros.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.370
Rhaenyra was a dragonrider whose mount was
Syrax.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:03.840
Rhaenyra had her family's Valyrian looks,
wearing her silver-gold hair in a long braid

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.000
in the manner of Queen Visenya Targaryen.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.540
Beautiful as a child, Rhaenyra was later declared
by her uncle, Prince Daemon Targaryen, to

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.640
be the most beautiful maiden in all the Seven
Kingdoms.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.650
Due to the lack of a male heir, Viserys designated
Rhaenyra as his successor.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:24.900
Therefore, Rhaenyra was the only female Targaryen
to lay claim to the Iron Throne in her own

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:25.900
right.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:31.810
After Rhaenyra's mother died, her father remarried
and had several sons by his second wife, Alicent

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.760
of House Hightower.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.720
Even so, Viserys still publicly expected his
daughter to succeed him, and when he died,

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.210
his official will even stated so.

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:45.720
However, Rhaenyra's younger half-brother,
Aegon, challenged her claim.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.110
He stated that the normal inheritance laws
of the Andals (which formed the basis of the

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:56.290
unified law code in Westeros) called for male-preference
primogeniture, meaning that a younger son

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.120
would rightfully inherit before an older daughter.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:04.020
At the time of her father's death, Rhaenyra
was on Dragonstone awaiting the birth of her

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.070
child.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:09.140
The greens in King's Landing ensured that
the news of Viserys's death did not reach

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:15.140
her until her own supporters in the Red Keep
were dead or imprisoned and Aegon II's coronation

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.940
had already occurred.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:21.750
This began a devastating civil war that tore
apart the Seven Kingdoms, known as The Dance

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:26.280
of the Dragons, as it was the only war in
which both sides had dragonriders.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:31.010
The war lasted for three years, and by the
time it came to an end nearly all of the Targaryen

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.930
dragons had been killed.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:37.789
The conflict also resulted in the death of
three of Rhaenyra's five sons, as well as

00:04:37.789 --> 00:04:39.680
the eldest son of Aegon II.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:45.730
Rhaenyra's personal sigil was the normal Targaryen
heraldry (a three-headed red dragon on a black

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:50.780
field), quartered with the moon-and-falcon
sigil of House Arryn (for her mother Aemma

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:56.860
Arryn), and the silver seahorse on sea green
of House Velaryon (for her first husband Laenor

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:02.860
Velaryon, as well as for the Velaryons in
general, who were among her major supporters).

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:06.759
During the Dance, her faction used her personal
heraldry as their battle-flag.

00:05:06.759 --> 00:05:11.669
While both sides lost much and more in the
war, it is a fact that the Blacks won the

00:05:11.669 --> 00:05:17.550
war and it is a fact that Rhaenyra even though
dead by the end of it, also won the war because

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:23.510
its her sons that got the throne not Aegon's,
and the Targaryen line continued through her,

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:29.789
meaning that present time Targaryens are descendants
of Rhaenyra and not of her half-brother Aegon.

00:05:29.789 --> 00:05:34.289
Next most prominent of the Blacks is the character
that did the most in this war, the character

00:05:34.289 --> 00:05:39.919
that is equally loved and hated in Westeros,
and the Blacks best warrior, general and commander,

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:42.310
the Rogue Prince - Daemon Targaryen.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:46.039
Daemon Targaryen also known as Prince of the
City, Lord Flea Bottom and the Rogue Prince

00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:51.620
had many titles throughout his life: Prince,
Ser, Commander of the City Watch, Master of

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:57.340
coin, master of laws, King of the stepstones
and the narrow sea, protector of the realm.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:02.340
Daemon was the most contoversial man of his
lifetime, an audacious rogue prince and adventuer

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.509
who seemed made of good and evil in equal
measure.

00:06:05.509 --> 00:06:10.129
There was never a man so loved and so reviled,
and at a same time, as he was.

00:06:10.129 --> 00:06:15.289
During the Dance of the Dragons, as the husband
of his niece Rhaenyra, he supported his wife's

00:06:15.289 --> 00:06:19.310
claim, and he was considered by many the most
dangerous man in Westeros.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:24.720
He was Rhaenyra's second husband, following
Ser Laenor Velaryon and she was his third

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:25.720
wife.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:29.740
Prince Daemon was the most experienced warrior
of his time and wielded the Valyrian steel

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.039
blade Dark Sister.

00:06:31.039 --> 00:06:35.931
A dragonrider whose dragon was Caraxes, Daemon
declared himself the King of the Stepstones

00:06:35.931 --> 00:06:37.449
and the Narrow Sea.

00:06:37.449 --> 00:06:43.120
After giving him 2 daughters, Daemon's second
wife Laena died in 120 AC, trying to birth

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.870
him a son who died as well.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:51.530
In 120 AC Daemon married again, this time
to his niece, Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:56.569
This marriage was performed suddenly without
the knowledge of King Viserys I Targaryen,

00:06:56.569 --> 00:07:01.599
and was scandalous since neither Laena nor
Laenor Velaryon, Daemon's previous wife and

00:07:01.599 --> 00:07:05.020
Rhaenyra's previous husband, had been dead
for six months.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:10.280
According to Mushroom, it was Daemon who arranged
the death of Laenor by paying Ser Correy to

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:14.229
kill him, thus making Rhaenyra available to
marry.

00:07:14.229 --> 00:07:20.539
Daemon and Rhaenyra had two sons together,
Prince Aegon the Younger born in 120 AC and

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:23.800
Prince Viserys, born in 122 AC.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:28.069
At the start of the civil war called the Dance
of the Dragons, Prince Daemon had more experience

00:07:28.069 --> 00:07:31.629
in warfare than all their foes combined.

00:07:31.629 --> 00:07:36.650
During Rhaenyra's rival coronation on Dragonstone,
Daemon placed the crown of King Jaehaerys

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:42.499
I Targaryen on the head of his wife, proclaiming
her queen and claiming himself Protector of

00:07:42.499 --> 00:07:43.590
the Realm.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:48.860
Daemon led the assault on Harrenhal, capturing
the ruined castle from its castellan.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:53.550
After hearing of the death of his stepson,
Prince Lucerys Velaryon, at the hands of his

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:59.360
nephew, Prince Aemond Targaryen,
Daemon, through his spymaster and former mistress

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:03.819
Mysaria, hired Blood and Cheese to murder
a son of Aegon II.

00:08:03.819 --> 00:08:05.349
Son for a son.

00:08:05.349 --> 00:08:10.310
Daemon abandoned Harrenhal when Aemond and
Criston began marching on the great castle

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:14.389
with a host of greens
Instead, Daemon flew Caraxes back to King's

00:08:14.389 --> 00:08:18.240
Landing and assisted Rhaenyra with capturing
the city.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:22.229
He made his niece and wife, Rhaenyra the Queen
of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:08:22.229 --> 00:08:26.889
His next and final act in the war and in his
life was the battle above the Gods Eye when

00:08:26.889 --> 00:08:32.150
he challenged King Aegon's brother and the
most prominent of the Greens, Aemond One-Eye,

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:37.260
which is the day both, the Blacks and the
Greens lost its best warriors and commanders.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:42.630
Aemond answered Daemon's challenge, arrived
on legendary dragon Vhagar and the most epic

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:45.380
battle of the entire war was about to start.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:50.500
When he climbed upon Caraxes, Daemon did not
fasten his chains that connected him.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:55.080
Since Daemon's dragon was a lot younger and
smaller than Aemond's, Daemon was quickly

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.690
hidden in clouds whilst Aemon looked for him.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:02.770
When Caraxes attacked Vhagar, she ripped upon
his stomach and tore one of his wings, but

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:07.150
then Caraxes fastened his jaws around her
throat in death grip.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:13.000
These injuries forced them both to cease flying
and as they tumbled to the water below, Daemon

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.060
dueled Aemond to the death.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:20.400
As he never fastened his saddle, Daemon stood
up on Caraxes and leapt at Aemond,

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.970
whereupon he drove his Dark Sister through
Aemond's eye and through his neck, just a

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:27.070
second before hitting the water.

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:32.570
The Battle Above the Gods Eye ended in the
deaths of both riders and both dragons.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.590
Daemon was forty-nine when he died.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:38.610
Unlike Aemond's body, however, Daemon's was
never found.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:43.360
Singers say that Daemon lived to spend the
rest of his days in secret with Nettles, but

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.320
most historians disagree.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:50.290
House of the Dragon will end this debate between
singers and historians and reveal why Daemon's

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:56.090
body was never found and did he really survive
and live his days out in peace with Nettles.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:59.340
The next prominent member of the Blacks was
Lord Stark.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:03.170
Cregan Stark, known as the Old Man of the
North, The Wolf of the North and The Wolf

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:07.430
of Winterfell, was the Lord of Winterfell
and head of House Stark during the Targaryn

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:08.890
civil war.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:13.900
Upon the death of King Viserys I Targaryen,
Rhaenyra's son Prince Jacaerys Velaryon flew

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:18.280
to Winterfell on his dragon Vermax to gain
the support of the Starks and the north for

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:21.150
his mother Rhaenyra Targaryen's claim to the
Iron Throne.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:26.150
The alliance, known as the Pact of Ice and
Fire, stated that a Targaryen princess, the

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:30.240
future firstborn daughter of Jacaerys, would
marry his son Rickon.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.750
Cregan pledged his support to the blacks during
the Dance of the Dragons.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:39.000
After Prince Jacaerys Velaryon secured the
allegiance of the North for his mother Rhaenyra

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:44.610
Targaryen, Lord Cregan Stark sent two thousand
soldiers known as the Winter Wolves south

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:48.870
commanded by his bannerman Lord Roderick Dustin
known as Roddy the Ruin to support the Queen's

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:54.550
claim while he remained in the North to gather
his own banners (due to the vastness of the

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.180
North this would take long).

00:10:56.180 --> 00:11:00.750
Rhaenyra was killed at Dragonstone by King
Aegon II Targaryen, however, but Cregan with

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:06.450
his army still marched south nontheless in
support of her son, Prince Aegon the Younger.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:11.130
The war continued between the supporters of
the dead queen and the king's remaining loyalists.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:16.720
Riverlands, the North and the Vale still supported
the claim of Rhaenyra's son, Aegon III, while

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:20.180
Aegon II only had the Stormlands army able
to defend him.

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:25.120
While Lord Stark moved south with his army
to overthrow Aegon II and place Rhaenyra's

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:30.160
son on the Iron Throne, Lord Borros Baratheon
was marching north with his own banners but

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:36.260
he was defeated on the Kingsroad by the riverlords
known as the Lads before Lord Stark arrived.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:40.390
Having failed to get the battle he wanted,
Stark nevertheless wanted to punish those

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.780
who had supported Aegon II.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:47.670
He moved his forces to claim King's Landing
where he found that Aegon II had been poisoned

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:50.190
and Aegon III was now king.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:55.390
Since he was aged eleven, a regency needed
to be established and several lords were vying

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:56.570
for power.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:12:00.640
With his formidable presense and character
as well as with his army, Lord Stark was the

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:02.700
most powerful man in King's Landing.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:08.030
With his newfound power, Lord Stark wanted
to punish those who had supported Aegon II

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.930
such as the Baratheons, the Lannisters and
the Hightowers.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:16.500
However, Lord Corlys Velaryon had already
sent envoys to Oldtown, Storm's End and Casterly

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.990
Rock to make peace.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:22.870
While word of the envoys was being waited
upon, there was another matter that Lord Stark

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:25.920
wanted to deal with: the assassination of
Aegon II.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:30.850
While he had believed that he had been a usurper
and had been riding south to oust him from

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:36.000
power, Lord Stark did not believe in murdering
him but rather in defeating him on the field

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.200
of battle.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:41.930
He declared that all those who had partaken
in the killing needed to be punished.

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:46.980
His troops arrested several people in the
capital, including Lord Velaryon, Lord Larys

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:51.580
Strong, the Master of Whisperers, and several
members of the Kingsguard.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:55.480
After these arrests were made, Lord Stark
was appointed Hand of the King by King Aegon

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.850
III.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:13:01.670
During the day that followed his appointment,
Lord Stark led the trials and execution of

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:06.500
the traitors, sending most to the Wall and
executing a member of the Kingsguard and Lord

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.200
Strong who refused to take the black.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:14.220
Following the traditions of House Stark, Lord
Cregan beheaded them both himself with Ice,

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.730
the Valyrian steel greatsword of the Starks.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:21.570
This event came to be known as the 'Hour of
the Wolf' or the 'Judgment of the Wolf'.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:26.260
Lord Velaryon escaped execution or sentence
when the king issued an edict that he was

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:30.390
to be spared and returned to his former dignity
as Lord of the Tides.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:36.720
Cregan married Alysanne Blackwood in exchange
for honoring Aegon III's pardon of Lord Corlys.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:41.320
Lord Stark resigned as Hand the following
day and left King's Landing for Winterfell.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:46.210
''The snows are falling in the North and my
place is at Winterfell.'' said Cregan explaining

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:50.410
why he can not stay at King's Landing
It was during Cregan's long reign as Lord

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:54.720
of Winterfell that House Stark's loyalty to
the Iron Throne (doubtful at best prior to

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:56.610
this) became a certainty.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:14:00.570
Neither Rhaenyra and her Blacks or Aegon II
and his Greens are remembered well in the

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:06.050
history of the Westeros and many argue that
neither side truly won at the end but it is

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:10.760
a fact that Rhaenyra's loyalists won the war
and Rhaenyra's children got the throne.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:14.460
Let me know your thoughts about everything:
the prequel, its characters, especially the

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:16.760
Blacks, in the comment section down below.

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:20.480
Also let me know which side you support in
this Targaryen civil war, the Blacks or the

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:21.570
Greens and why.

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:24.471
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed
this video and if you did make sure to give

00:14:24.471 --> 00:14:32.570
it a big thumbs up and I hope to see you in
the next one, peace!

